    "name": "Preamble – Agreement Definition",
    "text": "Reference is made to the agreement (the \"Agreement\") between PolyGram Records, Inc. (wPRI\") and you, as successor-in-interest to DeNovo Music Group, Inc. and Steemer Corporation, respectively, as amended."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1. Options to Extend Term",
    "text": "\"Grantor grants PRI four (4) separate options to extend the Term for addi tional Contract Periods (sometimes referred to as \"Option Periods\").\""
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2. Fourth Option Period Recording Obligation",
    "text": "2. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary expressed or implied in paragraph 2.02 of the Agreement, the Minimum Recording Obligation for the fourth Option Period, as added hereby, shall be for one (1) Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "3. Paragraph 3.06(b) – Live Album Composition",
    "text": "(b) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary expressed or implied in paragraph 3.06(a} above, and without limiting any of PRI's rights hereunder, it is understood and agreed that the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation for the first Option Period shall be comprised entirely of Master Recordings embodying Artist's \"live\" concert performances recorded while Artist was on tour in __ tb~ Soviet Union in Februa~y 1989 I as \"ell eSAtwo ~ 14< *,-- PolyGram Records. Inc 810 Seventh Avenue New York.. NY t0019 Telephone: (212) 333-8000 Tele~ 620985 Casablanca Mercury ~sK- FI:llydor FI:llyGram ClassiCS 2803C/ Wing P89-117 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001404 - 2 - ~f ,I ~ of \",~4Ci1b4ll pI( R~~ ~ '¥ NlIdT aQ~~~~~~~u~~P&e&.eed s~es embodying MB~~8ieMA performance~~_ Such first"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "3. Paragraph 3.06(b) – Live Album Definition",
    "text": "Such first Album a the Minimum Recording Obligation for the first Option Period shall sometimes hereinafter be referred to as the \"Live Album\"."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "4. Paragraph 4.01(a)(i) – Album Delivery Deadlines",
    "text": "4.01. ( (i) The first Album of the Minimu Recording Obligation in the Initial Perio, the first Album of the Minimum v-: ~ Recor Ing Obligation in each of the second . and third Option Periods, and the Album r__~~~__ comprIsIng the Minimum Recording Obligation for the fourth Option Period, if any, shall be delivered no later than one hundred twenty (120) days following commencement of such Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "4. Paragraph 4.01(a)(ii) – Live Album Delivery",
    "text": "(ii) The Live Album (Le., the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the first Option Period) shall be delivered no later than May 29, 1989."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "4. Paragraph 4.01(b)(i) – First Option Period Second Album",
    "text": "(b) (i) The second Album comprIsIng the remainder of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the first Option Period shall be delivered no earlier than January 15,· 1990 and no later than March ,- 30, 1990."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "4. Paragraph 4.01(b)(ii) – Other Second Albums",
    "text": "(ii) The second Album cornprlslng the remainder of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the Initial Period, and the second Album comprising the remainder of the Minimum Recording Obligation in each of the second and third Option Periods, if any, shall be delivered no earlier than six (6) months and no later than ten (10) months following delivery of the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the applicable Contract Period."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "5. Paragraph 4.01(e) – Inapplicability to First Option Album",
    "text": "(e) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary expressed or .implied in paragraph 4.0l(c) or Cd) above, the provisions of 2803C/ P89-117 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001405 - 3 - paragraph 4.01 (c) and/or 4.01 (d) shall not apply to the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation for the first Option Period hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(i) – Applicable Advances",
    "text": "(b) (i) With respect to each Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation, PRI shall pay to Grantor an Advance equal to the applicable amount set forth below."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(i) – Initial Period First Album Advance",
    "text": "The Advance payable with respect to the first Album of the Minimum RecoIding Obligation in the Initial Period ,...... shall be payable one-quarter (1/4) wi thin sixty (60) days (the \"First Sixty Days\") following the day of PRI' s receipt of this agreement I fully executed by Grantor and Artist, one-quarter (1/4) promptly following PRI's receipt of notice of commencement of recording, one-quarter (l/4) promptly following PRI S receipt of I notice of commencement of mixing such Album and the balance promptly following delivery of all Master Recordings and other materials required to be delivered pursuant to Articles 3 and 4 and paragraph 10.03 with respect to such Album, provided, however, that if Grantor commences to .- record such Album within the First Sixty Days, then the aggregate of the one-quarter (1/4) of the Advance payable within the First Sixty Days and the one-quarter (l/4) of the Advance payable on commencement of recording shall be payable promptly following PRI's receipt of Grantor's notice of commencement of recording such Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(i) – Option Period First Album Advances",
    "text": "The Advance payable with respect to the fi rst Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in each of the first through third Option Periods, if any, and with respect to the Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the fourth Opt ion Period, shall be paid one-quarter (1/4) on the date of commencement of the applicable Contract Period, one-quarter (1/4) promptly following PRI 's receipt of notice of commencement of recording, one-quarter (1/4) promptly following PRI's receipt of notice of commencem~nt of mixing the 2803C/ PS9-I17 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001406 - 4 - applicable Album and the balance promptly following delivery of all Master Recordings and other materials required to be delivered pursuant to Articles 3 and 4 and paragraph 10.03 with respect to such Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(i) – Second Album Advances",
    "text": "The Advance payable with respect to the second Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation in the Initial Period and each of the first through third Option Periods, if any, shall be paid one-half (1/2) promptly following PRI S receipt of notice I of commencement of recording, one-quarter (1/4) promptly following PRI's receipt of notice of commencement of mixing the applicable Album, and the balance prompt ly following delivery of all Master Recordings and other materials required to be delivered pursuant to Articles 3 and 4 and paragraph 10.03 with respect to such Album."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(ii) – Recording Costs",
    "text": "(ii) Grantor shall be responsible for the payment of all Recording Costs or other costs in connection with making Master Recordings."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "6. Paragraph 6.01(b)(ii) – Reimbursement and Deduction Rights",
    "text": "If PRl elects to pay any such costs for which Grantor is responsible, then PRI sha 11 have the right to demand reimbursement therefor from Grantor (and Grantor shall immediately make such reimbursement) and/or the right to deduct such costs from any and all monies payable hereunder, except mechanical royalty payments."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.11(a) – United States Audio-Visual Royalty",
    "text": "7.11. (a) With respect to Net Sales of Audio-Visual Devices sold by PRI for ~, .,.' ' - ~\"/'-- / //,,,.\" ...... ' /<'- 2803C/ P89-117 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001407 - 5 - distribution in the United States, a royalty of nineteen percent (19\\) of the lowest wholesale price, exclusive of excise. sales and similar taxes, payable by PRI's customers in respect of such Audio-Visual Device."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.11(b) – Specified Foreign Audio-Visual Royalty",
    "text": "(b) with respect to Net Sales of Audio-Visual Devices sold by PRI and/or its affiliates for distribution in the united Kingdom, West Germany, France, Canada, Benelux, Australia, New Zealand and Japan, a royalty of twelve percent (12\\) of the lowest wholesale price, exclusive of excise, sales and similar taxes, payable by PRI·s r' customers is respect of such Audio-Visual Device."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.11(c) – Other Foreign Audio-Visual Royalty",
    "text": "(c) With respect to Net Sales of Audio-Visual Devices sold by PRI and/or its affi liates for distribution outside of the United States and the territories referred to in paragraph 7.11(b) above, a royalty of ,.., p~r(l.,.P\")8i~l!t pereenl (~) of the lowest wholesale price, exclusive of excise, sales and similar taxes, payable by PRIls customers in respect of such Audio-Visual Device."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.12(a) – United States CD/Video Royalty",
    "text": "7.12. (a) With respect to Net Sales of Records sold by PRI for distribution in the Uni ted States in the form of CO/Videos, a royalty of twelve percent (12\\) of the CD/Video Royalty Base."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.12(b) – Foreign CD/Video Royalty",
    "text": "(b) With respect to Net Sales of Records sold by PRI and/or its affi liates for distribution outs ide the united States in the form of CD/videos, a royalty of twelve percent (12%) of the CD/Video Royalty Base multiplied by a fraction, the numerator of which is the royalty rate set forth in this agreement for Net Sales of disc Albums sold by PRI for distribution in the applicable country, and the denominator of which is the royalty rate set forth in this agreement for Net Sales of disc Albums sold by PRI for distribution in the United States."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.12(c) – CD/Video Royalty Base Definition",
    "text": "(c) The ·'CD/video Royalty Base\" shall mean the lowest wholesale price, exclusive of excise, sales L and similar taxes, payable by PRI's customers in respect 2803C/ P89-U7 CONFIDENTIAL UMG-MAL 001408 - 6 - of such CD/Video, less thirty-five percent (35\\) of such lowest wholesale price."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "7. Paragraph 7.12(c) – Container Charge and Free Goods",
    "text": "No Container Charge or automatic free goods (as set forth in paragraph 13.15(a)(H) below) shall apply in respect of CD/Videos."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "8. Concert Video Purchase",
    "text": "8. The parties acknowledge and agree that pursuant to a separate agreement dated as of April 3, 1989, PRI shall purchase from Red Star Entertainment Co., Ltd. a \"long-form· Audio-Visual Recording embodying your concert performances in the Soviet Union during February 1989 (the \"Concert Video·)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "8(a). Satisfaction of Production Obligation",
    "text": "(a) PRI' s purchase of the Concert video shall be deemed to satisfy any obligation PRI may have pursuant to paragraph 5.02(a)(ii) of the Agreement to produce an AudiO-Visual Recording in connection 'With the first Album of the Minimum Recording Obligation for the first Option PeriOd."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "8(b). Concert Video Exploitation Rights",
    "text": "(b) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary expressed or implied in paragraph 5.02(b) of the Agreement, PRI may exploit, or refrain from exploiting, the Concert Video as it deems appropriate in its sole discretion including, without limi tat ion , editing the Concert Video for promotional and/or commercial purposes and manufacturing and exploiting AudiO-Visual Devices and/or CD/Videos embodying the Concert Video or any portion thereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "8(c). Concert Video Costs and Recoupment",
    "text": "(c) All amounts paid by PRI in connection with the Concert Video, including, without limitation, the cost of purchasing the Concert Video from Red Star Entertainment Co., Ltd., and any editing costs and/or post-production costs incurred in connection with the Concert Video, shall be deemed to be Advances under the Agreement, provided that only fifty percent (50%) of such costs shall be recoupable from audio-only Record royalties accrued to your royalty account under the Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "9. Audio-Visual Devices Definition",
    "text": "(a) \"AUdio-Visual Devices\": All forms of reproductions of Audio-Visual Recordings, excluding CD/video, now or hereafter known, manufactured or distributed primarily for home and/or juke box use and/or use on or in means of transportation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "10. Paragraph 13.04(g) – CD/Video Definition",
    "text": "(g) ReDIVideo-: A Phonograph Record in laser-read compact disc form embodying Audio-Visual Recordings, which may, without limitation, include additional audio-only Sides."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "10. Paragraph 13.04(h) – Equivalent Definition",
    "text": "(h) As used herein, the phrase ·or equivalent- shall mean every form of pre-recorded tape, compact disc or any other Record equivalent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "11. Undefined Terms",
    "text": "11. All terms not defined herein shall have the same meaning given them in the Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "11. Ratification and Confirmation",
    "text": "Except as expressly or by necessary implication modified hereby, the te:rms of the Agreement are hereby ratif ied and confirmed without limitation or exception."
  }
]

