{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"You, as successor-in-interest to DeNovo Music Group, Inc. and Steemer Corporation, respectively\" uses \"respectively\" for a single addressee and two predecessor entities, leaving unclear which rights and obligations passed to the individual. It also leaves unstated whether \"you\" is the \"Grantor\", the \"Artist\", or both under the underlying Agreement.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
     {"issue": "The preamble merges the addressee into a single \"you\", yet operative paragraph 6.01(b)(i) (c012) conditions the first advance instalment on receipt of the agreement \"fully executed by Grantor and Artist\", treating them as two persons. The identification of the contracting party is therefore not squared with the operative payment trigger.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause says the Live Album \"shall be comprised entirely of Master Recordings embodying Artist's 'live' concert performances\" recorded in the Soviet Union, yet the same sentence continues \"as well as two ... recordings embodying ... performance[s]\", which cannot be reconciled with \"entirely\". The interlineated/garbled added words make the permitted content of the Live Album genuinely uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.52},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The list of albums subject to the 120-day deadline omits the first Album of the first Option Period, so it is arguable whether that omission is deliberate (because clause (ii) fixes a May 29, 1989 date) or an oversight. The garbled enumeration compounds which albums the 120-day rule reaches.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": "The fixed May 29, 1989 delivery date sits against paragraph 3.06(b) (c004), which requires the Live Album to consist of February 1989 Soviet concert recordings plus additional recordings; whether the date survives if the additional recordings are not then available is left unaddressed. Read with the 120-day rule in 4.01(a)(i) (c006) the two deadlines govern different albums, but the boundary depends on c004's content requirement.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The advance table is keyed to \"First Album\" through \"Ninth Album\" in sequence, but the operative text identifies albums by Contract Period, so matching a particular album to \"the applicable amount set forth below\" requires an inference the clause does not supply. If any period's albums are not delivered the sequence numbering becomes contestable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The first instalment is triggered by PRI's receipt of \"this agreement, fully executed by Grantor and Artist\", but the amendment is a 1989 letter while the advance relates to the Initial Period album under the 1985 Agreement, so \"this agreement\" is ambiguous as between the two documents. The \"First Sixty Days\" proviso then runs from that ambiguous date.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"All Recording Costs or other costs in connection with making Master Recordings\" pairs a defined term with an open-ended \"other costs\" catch-all whose reach (e.g. mixing, mastering, travel, video production) is undefined. The general words are not confined by any enumerated list.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": "Making Grantor responsible for all Recording Costs sits awkwardly with paragraph 6.01(b)(i) (c011-c014), under which PRI pays advances in instalments tied to commencement of recording and mixing, and with paragraph 8(c) (c027), under which PRI's own video costs become Advances. Whether the advances are the exclusive funding source is not resolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Any and all monies payable hereunder, except mechanical royalty payments\" leaves \"hereunder\" ambiguous as between this amendment letter and the underlying Agreement, and the single carve-out invites an expressio unius argument about other protected payments. The scope of the deduction right therefore turns on words the clause does not define.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]}
]}

